[I] Fan controller for AMD graphics cards running the amdgpu driver on Linux

[T] amdgpu-fan is a Python daemon that controls the fans of AMD graphics
[T] cards using the amdgpu driver on Linux. It reads the GPU temperatures
[T] from sysfs and sets the fan speed according to a configurable
[T] temperature to speed curve.

[U] https://github.com/zzkW35/amdgpu-fan

[A] Amdgpu-fan Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

